<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 20:10:55 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Russian strikes leave hundreds of thousands without power</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-russian-strikes-leave-hundreds-of-thousands-without-power</link><description>
Hundreds of thousands of Ukrainians were left without electricity on Sunday following Russian airstrikes targeting the country's energy infrastructure. Moscow has intensified its attacks as winter approaches, leaving residents in Kyiv and other parts of the country struggling with power cuts as temperatures continue to drop. Clemence Waller reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a894976-db94-11f1-846b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-171056-171236-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a894976-db94-11f1-846b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-171056-171236-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3fdd8a5e-db94-11f1-b79f-6343e38d3fa8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:59:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gadi Eisenkot receives mandate to form government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government</link><description>
Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has officially been tasked with forming the country's next government, following a formal announcement by President Isaac Herzog. He now has up to six weeks to negotiate with potential coalition partners and secure a parliamentary majority. While an alliance with Arab Israeli parties appears to be the easiest option mathematically, it remains politically sensitive. Eisenkot must now navigate difficult negotiations to build a coalition capable of replacing Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65b815e2-db93-11f1-9ee7-4943b8d2bb10</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:58:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Spain's Alcaraz beats error-prone Shelton to win Paris Masters for first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261108-spain-s-alcaraz-beats-error-prone-shelton-to-win-paris-masters-for-first-time</link><description>
Spanish tennis star Carlos Alcaraz avenged his loss to American player Ben Shelton in the US Open in September as he inched ahead of his rival Sunday to win the Paris Masters for the first time. It was Shelton's first defeat in a Masters final.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7a1efda-db91-11f1-95fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/f75fa6fa8ded7fbfacd31db319351a05d3ba1ad3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7a1efda-db91-11f1-95fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/f75fa6fa8ded7fbfacd31db319351a05d3ba1ad3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e86e877a-db91-11f1-b8e6-9355be3483f4</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:31:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7a1efda-db91-11f1-95fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/f75fa6fa8ded7fbfacd31db319351a05d3ba1ad3.jpg">© Dimitar Dilkoff, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: US midterms 'Blue Wave', French protests and Dakar Youth Olympics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-the-week-in-pictures-trump-midterms-debacle-french-protests-dakar-youth-olympics</link><description>
From the Democratic Party's big wins in the US midterm elections to France's ongoing student-led protests and the first Olympic sports event held on African soil, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6cb3870-db7e-11f1-a1cc-330d38f8a0f8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:21:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg">© Kieran Cleeves, OIS/IOC via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tech 24</category><title>US voters reject AI data centres: could the backlash spread to France?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261108-us-voters-reject-ai-data-centres-could-the-backlash-spread-to-france</link><description>
In Tuesday’s US midterm elections, voters weighed in on more than 40 local measures on data centres, and sided against them in all but one. With Democrats taking control of Congress in January and new governors in Texas and Georgia calling for moratoriums, the AI building boom faces its toughest political test yet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4636e71a-db80-11f1-a6d8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-WB-TECH24-MIDTERMS-DATA-CENTRE-FALLOUT.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4636e71a-db80-11f1-a6d8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-WB-TECH24-MIDTERMS-DATA-CENTRE-FALLOUT.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c73f8e88-db81-11f1-8ff5-dbf7c48ee3c6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:36:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Peter O'BRIEN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens</link><description>
One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6735dcac-db7e-11f1-b6b0-a3bc1c7deeec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:22:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland in shock after 6 killed in Krakow far-right shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting</link><description>
Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital. FRANCE 24 journalist Adrien Sariat reports from Poland.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">620ad868-db7e-11f1-9f57-c1ea51b6f7a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:21:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French skipper wins Route du Rhum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-skipper-wins-route-du-rhum</link><description>
French sailor Tom Laperche has won the Route du Rhum, setting a new record in the transatlantic yacht race. The 29-year-old crossed the finish line in Guadeloupe on his first attempt, beating the previous 2022 record by around six hours. A remarkable debut in one of sailing's toughest competitions!
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83ffbb5a-db7e-11f1-adef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150723-150909-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83ffbb5a-db7e-11f1-adef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150723-150909-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8908bf7a-db7e-11f1-a60f-8bcd096c4ca7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:20:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mourning in Poland after mass shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting</link><description>
Poland has launched a terrorism investigation after a deadly shooting left six people dead and 16 injured. The 24-year-old Polish suspect was reportedly fascinated by far-right ideologies. Authorities are investigating the possible extremist motive as Krakow's main square remains sealed. Two days of national mourning have been declared for the victims.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b127f486-db7d-11f1-8be9-85907240b2be</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:18:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe will take part in US-mediated Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, French FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says</link><description>
France will participate in the upcoming Abu Dhabi peace talks on ending the Ukraine war, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said Sunday, adding that Europeans will be represented at the summit. The talks will take place under US mediation on Tuesday and Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3ba58f6-db7a-11f1-9002-631a5aa7e06e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:16:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg">© Megan Varner, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo urges men to respect wives amid Latin American femicide crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-urges-husbands-to-respect-wives-amid-femicide-crisis-across-latin-america</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV urged men to respect their wives as he wrapped up the first leg of his 12-day tour of Latin America. The region recorded nearly 20,000 instances of women being killed over the past five years alone, most of them murdered by a current or former partner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e95bad06-db7e-11f1-94ec-63ab1173e7a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:15:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg">© Rodrigo Arangua, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>‘10 times more painful’: Menstrual disorders fuel calls to ban tear gas at French protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261108-abnormal-menstraution-periods-fuel-calls-ban-tear-gas-french-protests-police</link><description>
French police have made extensive use of tear gas during protests that have roiled France in recent weeks, sometimes causing grievous injuries. Thousands of accounts of women experiencing acutely painful periods and increased bleeding are further challenging assumptions that the chemical irritant carries only minor consequences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a664e012-da11-11f1-ab05-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3LF967.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a664e012-da11-11f1-ab05-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3LF967.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3240f6a-d9fc-11f1-ac74-9777b0a3a97d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 11:53:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a664e012-da11-11f1-ab05-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3LF967.jpg">© Ed Jones, AFP</source><dc:creator>Benjamin DODMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>2026 Dakar Youth Olympic Games: Golden Double for Senegal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261108-2026-dakar-youth-olympic-games-golden-double-for-senegal</link><description>
Senegal won two gold medals in beach wrestling at the Youth Olympic Games in Dakar. Elisabeth Diatta won gold in the -55 kg category, the host country’s first gold medal at the Youth Olympic Games. Her compatriot Maguette Diop followed suit, taking gold in the -80 kg category.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed16cfe6-db62-11f1-971d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/JOJ-DAKAR-2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed16cfe6-db62-11f1-971d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/JOJ-DAKAR-2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48704b16-db35-11f1-84de-35ca72a4bcea</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:56:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Diwali: Over one billion people mark victory of light over darkness</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness</link><description>
Diwali celebrations began on Sunday, with people across India and the global diaspora gathering to mark one of the most important festivals in the Hindu tradition. In Ayodhya, believed to be the birthplace of Lord Rama, the deity celebrated during the festival, festivities included performances based on the Hindu epic Ramayana, laser and light shows, live music, fireworks and drone displays.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cac0a34c-db60-11f1-b422-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111252-111423-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cac0a34c-db60-11f1-b422-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111252-111423-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cfba9c7c-db60-11f1-9841-59074deecd2b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:46:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paraguay: Senate impeached Peña rather than accept his offer to resign</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261108-paraguay-senate-impeached-pe%C3%B1a-rather-than-accept-his-offer-to-resign</link><description>
Paraguay's ousted president, Santiago Peña, has been charged over the collapse of Ueno Bank. Initially placed under house arrest, he has since been transferred to a military facility for his own safety. Nearly three million customers were locked out of their accounts after regulators seized control of the online bank. Repayments are now under way, but protests continue as customers demand access to their money. Peña denies any wrongdoing. Jack Pownall reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97992746-db60-11f1-b875-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111033-111218-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97992746-db60-11f1-b875-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111033-111218-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c89fc9e-db60-11f1-b55f-b7e2ef7616a9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:42:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Israeli president officially tasks Eisenkot with forming government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-netanyahu-coalition-government-elections</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Sunday officially tasked ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot with trying to form a government after neither Eisenkot's bloc nor that or incumbent Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu won a clear majority in Israel's October 28 elections. Eisenkot now has up to six weeks to form a coalition government. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments from the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f9136bc-db58-11f1-b6e9-1d122f9c1034</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:47:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Louise NORDSTROM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump wants UFC fighters as assistants</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-wants-ufc-fighters-as-assistants</link><description>
After a series of combative press briefings between the Trump administration and journalists, the US president surprised many by reportedly offering Dana White, the head of the Ultimate Fighting Championship (UFC) and a longtime friend, the role of White House press secretary. Trump praised White as a “violent fighter and warrior”, but US media reports say he has already turned down the offer. Was it a punchy choice by the president or simply a punchline? Jack Pownall takes a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad7ce2ee-db58-11f1-b2b1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-101159-101400-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad7ce2ee-db58-11f1-b2b1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-101159-101400-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b289ad26-db58-11f1-ae95-2ff3ce4ecc5e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:44:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel's Arab-led parties gain influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence</link><description>
Arab-led parties have endorsed Gadi Eisenkot despite his ruling out a coalition with them. Their support is driven by a shared goal: removing Benjamin Netanyahu from power. But could these parties ultimately hold the balance of power in forming Israel's next government? Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dec0c3da-db57-11f1-b79b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100714-100924-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dec0c3da-db57-11f1-b79b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100714-100924-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3c19d0a-db57-11f1-afce-7d507642ff15</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:43:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gaza: Heavy rain inundates thousands of tents</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents</link><description>
Heavy rainfall has flooded thousands of tents sheltering displaced Palestinians across the Gaza Strip, including in Deir al-Balah. Residents say overflowing sewage has mixed with the floodwater, further worsening already dire living conditions. Families are struggling to salvage their belongings, building makeshift earthen barriers and trying to drain the water by hand. Many have seen essential items soaked and rendered unusable, adding to the hardship faced by those already displaced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25796fa2-db58-11f1-946f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100942-101123-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25796fa2-db58-11f1-946f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100942-101123-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2ac0b998-db58-11f1-a8f1-2946bdd1dc7c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:42:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Poland launches terrorism probe into mass shooting in Krakow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-poland-launches-terrorism-probe-into-krakow-mass-shooting</link><description>
